{
 "thread": "srOY12BfxFw",
 "subject": "Reordering bars by multiple variables",
 "messages_listed": 4,
 "last_activity": "2017-12-20T04:51:25Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "SnizSzv6BQAJ",
   "from": "jyr...@gmail.com",
   "author": "3ada5bc98608b5f2",
   "date": "2017-12-18T01:41:46Z",
   "subject": "Reordering bars by multiple variables",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Say, I want to rearrange the bars in my plot by a variable, I can do something like<div><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> reorder</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">name</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> variable1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></font><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br></div><div>But how would I go about using two variables for reordering? To first order by variable1, then by variable2?</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Bqc8PN36BQAJ",
   "from": "jyr...@gmail.com",
   "author": "3ada5bc98608b5f2",
   "date": "2017-12-18T01:53:22Z",
   "subject": "Re: Reordering bars by multiple variables",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Turns out this does the job:<div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> reorder</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">reorder</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">name</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> variable2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> variable1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></font><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Not the prettiest looking solution but it works.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Monday, 18 December 2017 03:41:46 UTC+2, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jyr...@gmail.com</a>  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Say, I want to rearrange the bars in my plot by a variable, I can do something like<div><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> reorder</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">name</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> variable1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></font><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br></div><div>But how would I go about using two variables for reordering? To first order by variable1, then by variable2?</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
